<sup><b>1</b></sup> I cried unto the Lord with my voice; with my voice unto the Lord did I make my supplication.<br />
<sup><b>2</b></sup> I poured out my complaint before him; I shewed before him my trouble.<br />
<sup><b>3</b></sup> When my spirit was overwhelmed within me, then thou knewest my path. In the way wherein I walked have they privily laid a snare for me.<br />
<sup><b>4</b></sup> I looked on <i>my</i> right hand, and beheld, but <i>there was</i> no man that would know me: refuge failed me; no man cared for my soul.<br />
<sup><b>5</b></sup> I cried unto thee, O Lord: I said, Thou <i>art</i> my refuge <i>and</i> my portion in the land of the living.<br />
<sup><b>6</b></sup> Attend unto my cry; for I am brought very low: deliver me from my persecutors; for they are stronger than I.<br />
<sup><b>7</b></sup> Bring my soul out of prison, that I may praise thy name: the righteous shall compass me about; for thou shalt deal bountifully with me. <br />
